WEBVTT

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:08.720
A-A request from outside the school?

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:09.440
Yeah.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:12.120
Apparently they want us to do a cheer

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:16.700
<b>Kaminoki Festival</b>

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.340
at the opening ceremony 
for a local festival.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:16.700
Wow...

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.520
Isn't it amazing?

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.440
You look so happy, Kohane-chan.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:26.570
Well, yeah! We get to cheer 
in front of everyone again.

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:30.400
I'm looking forward to i— 
Ow, ow, ow, ow...

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.520
You're sorta creepy...

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:46.020
<b>Anima Yell!</b>

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.850
It's pretty amazing that we got a request 
from outside the school, though.

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:08.940
<b>Kaminoki Festival
Opening Ceremony</b>

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:10.810
Before we knew it, the 
rumors about our cheering

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:13.830
had even spread to public servants.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:17.030
Yeah, that's not it.

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:20.040
Apparently the event organizer's daughter

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.280
had gone to see Basketball-senpai's game.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.530
So it's because of the 
basketball team again.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.870
I'm not sure if we'll ever be able 
to fully pay Basketball-senpai back.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.670
We need to go thank her later!

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.670
<i>I sense the presence of the 
cheer association again...</i>

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:43.680
<b>Kaminoki Festival
 Opening Ceremony!</b>

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:43.680
<b>We'll have food stalls!
Candied apples
French fries
Shaved ice
Frankfurters
and much more!</b>

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:43.680
<b>Episode 6: Super Exciting 
Double Base Thigh Stand!</b>

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:43.680
This is our first activity outside of school, 
so we should make it the best we can.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:48.670
Since our venue is outdoors this time,
 let's work on our formation.

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:51.980
We'll split back and forth
and do some line dancing.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:56.700
Let's do it! Transformation!

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:58.820
Why are you <i>trans</i>forming?

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:01.240
<b>Transformation</b>

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:00.780
That might not be a bad idea.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.010
You actually accepted that?!

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:05.000
Transforming by changing our 
outfits during the performance...

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.040
That would be flashy.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.110
Flashy, huh?

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:09.640
Oh, yeah. Stunts...

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:10.710
Stunts?

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:14.640
If we're outdoors, we could 
actually try doing some stunts.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.210
Stunts! I want to do them!

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:21.230
The one to go on top would be 
either Kohane-san or Kotetsu-san.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:23.000
Oh, you go right ahead, Kohane-chan.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:23.840
Me?!

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:27.600
Well, you know... I just started.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:31.100
<i>Stare...</i>

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:31.100
And it's not by much, 
but I'm just a tiny bit taller.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:34.780
A-And my weight... well...

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.400
Don't make her actually say it.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:40.610
What determines who goes on top 
is your height, not your weight.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:43.820
There isn't much of a 
difference between you two.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:49.080
<i>I really want to do stunts,</i>

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:52.250
<i>but I'm scared of heights.</i>

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.000
M-Me!

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:01.580
I-I really want to be on top!

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:04.890
<i>Kohane's agreeing to something 
that's gonna be trouble again...</i>

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.320
I-I'll do my best to fly!

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:08.760
High into the sky!

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:09.980
You won't be flying.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:11.310
I won't?!

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:18.020
<b>Double base thigh stand</b>

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:14.200
This is our first attempt at doing stunts,

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:18.020
so we'll be doing an easier stunt called 
the double base thigh (sai) stand.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:19.160
Rhinoceros (sai)?!

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.030
Not that "sai."

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.150
It actually means "thigh" in English.

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:27.440
You'll be standing on the 
thighs of the two bases.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:30.060
That's the double base thigh stand.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:31.150
And then...

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:32.040
Hi-yah!

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.610
Do you just want to fly?

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:36.810
Let's give it a try.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.830
The bases will be Kotetsu-san and myself.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:41.560
Uki-san, you'll be the spotter.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:45.100
Shouldn't I be the other base with you?

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.930
We're about the same height.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:50.080
The spotter basically 
acts as the commander

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:52.330
who keeps an eye on everything 
and gives directions.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:54.180
I believe that'll be 
perfect for you, Uki-san.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:57.560
That seems like a lot of responsibility...

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:01.960
You get to be up close and personal with 
the person on top and hold her up.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:04.320
O-Okay! Let's do this!

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:08.430
As the other base, Kotetsu-san, 
please follow my lead.

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:09.780
O-Okay...

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:14.170
This is called a lunge.

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:17.180
Kotetsu-san, please come over here.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:22.150
You'll be mirroring me,

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:25.120
so face forward and bend your right leg.

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:27.180
L-Like this?

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:30.350
Point your toes away from your body.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:32.620
Your knee will also be facing the same way.

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:39.000
Your other leg, including your knee 
and toes, will be facing forward.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:43.790
If the bases have good posture, 
the person on top will be secure.

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:44.970
Let's do our best.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:48.950
Sorry to keep you waiting, Kohane-san.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:51.700
It's finally your turn.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:53.220
Okay!

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:58.580
The top person steps here, 
right on the top of the thighs.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:00.860
Once the top person is up,

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:03.290
we, as bases, will wrap our 
arms around her knees.

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:04.380
Okay.

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:09.560
Uki-san, you'll hold on to her sides 
and keep supporting her throughout.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:10.760
Okay.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:13.760
Stunts aren't about strength.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.770
What's important is getting 
our timing together.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:20.280
Let's practice so we can perfect 
our timing and make sure

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:22.010
everything goes smoothly.

00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:22.790
Okay!

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:27.640
We'll be moving with the command 
of "one, two, down, up."

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:31.740
Are you sure I can step on 
you guys with my shoes on?

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:34.700
One, two, down, up!

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:35.420
<i>I'm sorry, you two!</i>

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:41.520
Thighs of steel. They're not soft.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:43.090
What was that?

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:48.100
We actually did it?

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:52.410
I'm gonna fall!

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:53.140
Whoa!

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.400
Well, I guess it couldn't go that easily.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:57.640
Of course not.

00:06:58.360 --> 00:06:59.900
What's wrong, Kohane?

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:01.800
Did you hurt anything?

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:03.270
Kohane-chan!

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:05.580
It's just like that one day...

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:06.990
Is your life flashing before you?!

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:08.780
Hizume-chan, calm down!

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:22.880
<i>I'm going to be okay.</i>

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:25.940
<i>Everyone's with me.</i>

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:28.230
<i>They'll support me.</i>

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:34.080
<i>Is she really...</i>

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:35.900
<i>Should we take her to the nurse's office?</i>

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:38.780
Okay! I'm gonna do this!

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:40.310
Let's do these stunts!

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:43.610
I'm not sure what's going on,

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:46.160
but I'm glad she's being 
positive about it now.

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:48.720
Let's do the stunt again!

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:50.510
All of us together!

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:53.380
Wait, Kohane! We aren't ready yet!

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.930
This is your fault, Kohane.

00:07:57.930 --> 00:07:58.830
Right...

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:01.580
So that's why these mats are here.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:04.960
The most important thing 
about cheering is

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.840
to not get hurt and not hurt anyone else.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:12.760
For that, we need to always keep 
safety first when we're practicing.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:14.010
I see.

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:17.000
<i>If some awful accident were to happen,</i>

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.920
<i>the other girls would be emotionally scarred.</i>

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:20.560
<i>That'll split up the team...</i>

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:24.560
<i>They won't want to cheer anymore, 
and I'll be all alone again!</i>

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:27.720
Hey, Hizume... Come back to us.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:33.530
Actually, I've already 
thought up some choreography.

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:35.600
Wow, that's amazing!

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:38.410
Let's all brush up our movements, 
using this as a starting point.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.700
Hey, I like this song!

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:44.910
I know this song, too.

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:46.440
It's a great song.

00:08:55.910 --> 00:09:00.160
Um... Who's this dancing with you?

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:01.320
My older brother.

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:07.560
Her brother... was actually pretty good.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.820
His moves were so crisp.

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:13.780
Please stop checking out my brother 
and check out the dance moves.

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:17.700
I liked the part where you 
spin your arm, like this.

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:23.200
Maybe it would look nice if we 
staggered our timing a bit.

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:28.680
I think it's going to be hard to 
synchronize the line dancing...

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:31.470
<i>It's no use... He left such an impact</i>

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:35.130
<b>Bro                     Bro                     Bro                     Bro                     Bro</b>

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:34.820
<i>that everything I think of gets 
replayed with him in my head.</i>

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:37.590
Okay, let's give it a try.

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:39.340
We'll start off slow.

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:41.630
One, two, three, four,

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:43.970
five, six, seven, eight.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:46.850
Two, two, three, four, five...

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.050
When moving in formation,

00:09:49.050 --> 00:09:51.610
move calmly while staying 
aware of your surroundings.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:56.200
Also, make sure you keep smiling.

00:09:57.780 --> 00:09:59.370
One more time.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:03.660
One, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight.

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:07.740
Two, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:11.590
Three, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight.

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:15.920
Four, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:15.210
<i>Looking around...</i>

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:18.970
<i>Kohane's too worried about her surroundings, 
and her movements are odd.</i>

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:20.030
Five, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight.

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:24.340
Six, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:26.620
<i>Hizume's movements are so smooth that 
I can't follow them with my eye!</i>

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:32.440
So that's basically what the 
choreography looks like.

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:35.190
As for personal goals 
everyone should work on...

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:39.150
Kotetsu-san, be a little more 
confident in your calls.

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:40.610
O-Okay!

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:43.600
Uki-san, try to not be so embarrassed.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:45.910
R-Right... I know.

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:48.120
As for Kohane-san...

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:52.220
Try to calm down a bit.

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:55.460
What?! But we're supposed to hype things up!

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:58.260
All right, let's start again from the top.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:02.490
One, two, three, four, five, six...

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:08.330
Okay, that's enough for today.

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:10.550
Let's also practice on our own at home.

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:13.650
I wonder if I can remember it all...

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:16.890
This is why we have 
cheerleading notes.

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:18.200
Cheerleading notes?!

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:19.480
That sounds great!

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:21.410
It's just a normal notebook.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:26.410
You write down what you did today, 
choreography notes, and your goals.

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:32.910
Along with that, I'll send that 
video from earlier to all of you.

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:35.670
You just want to show off 
your brother, don't you?

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:41.300
<b>Days until showtime:</b>

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:41.300
<b>Remember the formation.
Don't forget to smile
Be aware of your surroundings
Listen to the music</b>

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:39.950
Now that we have our choreography, 
there's nothing to be afraid of!

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:41.300
Let's keep practicing!

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.950
We only have a week until 
showtime, so let's make sure

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:45.870
we learn everything by then.

00:11:45.870 --> 00:11:47.190
One week!

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:50.870
What's the matter, Kohane-chan?

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:52.690
Something that might get in our way...

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:55.190
<b>This week's weather</b>

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:54.410
There.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:55.190
<b>Saturday
Rain</b>

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:58.350
We'll just have to incorporate 
some rain dancing into our cheer!

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:00.940
Rain dancing will have the 
opposite effect of what we want!

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:03.820
<b>Days until showtime:</b>

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:13.830
<b>Days until showtime:</b>

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:18.340
<b>Days until showtime:</b>

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:23.840
<b>Days until showtime:</b>

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:28.350
<b>Days until showtime:</b>

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:38.250
A white shadow...

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:40.460
In the A/V room no one's using...

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:43.070
Don't you also hear random 
piano sounds over there?

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:46.230
<i>The ghost rumors are 
spreading even further...</i>

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:52.000
Tomorrow's finally showtime!!

00:12:59.990 --> 00:13:04.440
So this is the event venue where the 
cheer association's going to perform.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:08.260
You must be the Tsutsujiyama 
Elementary baton twirling club.

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:10.410
Your rehearsal is in thirty minutes.

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:12.490
Oh, there they are.

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:12.220
The changing rooms are right over there,

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:14.040
so go ahead and get changed.

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:14.270
Hey!

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:15.320
Okay.

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:16.040
Inukai-sensei!

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:18.270
Sensei, perfect timing!

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:22.490
She sensed something 
troublesome and tried to flee!

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:23.850
What kind of adult is she?!

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:26.280
Sensei, please wait!

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:32.110
The event organizer said they 
wanted to talk to an adult.

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:33.870
Thank you for showing up.

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:37.550
We don't actually get an adviser 
as an association, so...

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:40.200
You should just join our club, Sensei!

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:43.080
Then we'd actually have five members.

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:45.470
What are you talking about?

00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:48.200
I'd rather die than wear 
a cheerleading uniform.

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:49.220
Die?!

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:53.140
Well, I talked to them,

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:56.700
so the rest is up to you guys. 
I'll be watching from the stands.

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:58.380
Thank you very much!

00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:00.900
Hello, Kaminoki High School 
cheer association.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:03.020
Please get set up for your rehearsal.

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:04.150
Yes, sir!

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:06.150
<b>Girls' Changing Room</b>

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:09.110
Huh?

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:11.450
I can't find my uniform.

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:13.080
Did you actually forget it?!

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:18.600
I couldn't have! I was so excited 
seeing my uniform last night...

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:23.020
that I slept in it.

00:14:36.650 --> 00:14:39.060
Okay, please begin your rehearsals.

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:40.470
Yes, sir!

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:48.030
We're the Kaminoki High 
School cheer association.

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:50.600
Thank you for having us today!

00:14:54.400 --> 00:15:00.250
W! E! L! C! O! M! E! Welcome!

00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:02.630
<i>This takes me back...</i>

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:05.630
<i>We used to rehearse like this all the time.</i>

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:10.950
<i>Usually, the smaller girls would get too 
worked up and drain all their stamina...</i>

00:15:15.050 --> 00:15:19.180
Kohane-san! Don't go 
all-out during rehearsal!

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:22.190
Okay, we're good.

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:25.940
Thank you very much.

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:25.940
Thank you!

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:33.370
That wasn't what I imagined at all.

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:35.230
The place felt so big.

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:36.950
The seats were so close to us.

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:39.470
Th-That was okay, right?

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:42.460
Oh! Yeah, everything's A-OK!

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:47.460
It feels so nice dancing on an actual stage!

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:51.470
Make sure you don't move too 
far forward and fall off.

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:54.440
I'm curious about the other performances.

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:53.850
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:57.160
<i>I'm not sure if I had the 
dance right the entire time...</i>

00:15:57.160 --> 00:15:59.720
U-Um, I'm sorry.

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:03.040
I was so bad...

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:04.850
Huh? You were?

00:16:04.850 --> 00:16:07.860
I-I'm pretty sure I was!

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:10.240
I only remember the sky being pretty

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:13.390
and the fact that we were 
so close to the seats.

00:16:13.390 --> 00:16:14.780
<i>That's worse than me!</i>

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:18.160
I-I couldn't do it at all like we practiced,

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:20.780
and I was holding you all back...

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:23.040
Huh? That's not true.

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:26.650
No, I know better than anyone else.

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:29.420
I was completely out of 
stamina when we finished, too.

00:16:29.970 --> 00:16:33.050
I forgot to smile when 
we changed formations...

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:36.080
I'm sure it was nothing 
like how you three looked

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:39.060
when you were cheering for 
the basketball team.

00:16:39.370 --> 00:16:40.660
Kotecchan!

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.160
Isn't this great?!

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:44.440
Did you hear a word I just said?

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:49.360
I mean, the sun's sparkling in 
the sky, and the weather's great!

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:52.780
And we'll be cheering with all 
four of us for the first time!

00:16:53.590 --> 00:16:55.360
B-But...

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:59.040
I wasn't able to kick high enough, 
and I wasn't even smiling,

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:00.780
and my timing was off!

00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:02.500
That's more than I was expecting...

00:17:03.030 --> 00:17:04.920
You're thinking about this way too hard!

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:06.500
Bap! Bap!

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:10.120
So today, we don't have 
to worry how well we do.

00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:13.580
Let's just have fun! That way, 
we'll be smiling naturally!

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:19.320
This is your first time, Kotecchan.

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:21.770
The last thing I want is 
for you to not have fun!

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:26.560
Well, all of you are doing 
stunts for the first time.

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.970
I just want everyone to have fun.

00:17:28.970 --> 00:17:32.950
But Kohane-san may have a point.

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:38.580
If the people performing are nervous, 
it'll come across to the audience, too.

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:41.280
Empty your mind, and imagine 
you're having the most fun

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:46.560
of anyone in the venue... no, 
f anyone in the whole world.

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:50.170
Oh, come on. That's crazy, Hizume-chan.

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:51.960
We have a shining example right here.

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:52.890
Ah...

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:53.670
<b>Convinced</b>

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:04.200
Everyone else seems so confident.

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:07.150
This is pretty nerve-wracking.

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:08.680
Y-Yeah...

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:11.690
<i>That was World Flight Circle.</i>

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:16.950
<i>Next, we have a performance from the 
Kaminoki High School cheer association.</i>

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:20.570
<i>Please enjoy their cute, refreshing dance!</i>

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:33.960
It's nice to meet you!

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:36.710
We're the Kaminoki High 
School cheer association!

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:38.840
Thanks for having us today!

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:42.380
<i>Typical Hizume... She's so calm.</i>

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:47.560
W! E! L! C! O! M! E!

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:48.940
Welcome!

00:18:49.490 --> 00:18:52.690
<i>She may look calm, but I guess 
she's a bit nervous, too!</i>

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:56.280
<i>Let me hear your voices!</i>

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:59.240
<i>Let's go on an adventure!</i>

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:01.550
<i>Let's start doing something fun!</i>

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:04.450
<i>I want to play, play, play, play!</i>

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:07.040
<i>I wanna joy, joy, joy!</i>

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:09.840
<i>Pop, baby!</i>

00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:10.670
<i>Huh?</i>

00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:13.170
<i>Joy, joy, joy...</i>

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:16.590
<i>Everything doesn't seem as 
spread out as it did at rehearsals.</i>

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:19.840
<i>That's right...</i>

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:22.840
<i>I'm not up here alone.</i>

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:27.350
<i>Everyone's here with me.</i>

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:31.050
<i>I was so nervous,</i>

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:34.150
<i>I didn't even realize that.</i>

00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:52.210
<i>K-Kohane-chan looks like she's 
having so much fun...</i>

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:53.250
Let's go!

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:25.320
<i>I don't feel her weight at all...</i>

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:29.580
<i>It's like she's grown wings.</i>

00:20:38.740 --> 00:20:40.710
<i>Er, so much for her wings.</i>

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:49.100
<i>That was the Kaminoki High 
School cheer association!</i>

00:20:49.990 --> 00:20:52.140
Thank you very much!

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:57.070
Wasn't that amazing?!

00:20:57.070 --> 00:20:58.430
Y-Yeah...

00:20:58.430 --> 00:21:00.670
Kohane was right there, 
but she was so light!

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:02.110
I-I felt that way, too!

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:05.110
It's probably because 
our timing was perfect.

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:07.160
That was so much fun!

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:08.620
You're so heavy!

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:11.160
I was so nervous!

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:13.560
My heart's still pounding!

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:15.880
I totally messed up!

00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:18.580
No worries. We couldn't tell at all.

00:21:20.390 --> 00:21:24.140
<i>I see... We're all the same.</i>

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:27.970
Heya. Good job.

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:30.110
I brought you guys refreshments.

00:21:30.110 --> 00:21:31.360
Sensei!

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:34.330
Thank you very much!

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:37.900
Sensei, what did you think 
about our performance?

00:21:40.720 --> 00:21:43.660
Yeah, it looks like you worked really hard.

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:46.280
We could really tell that 
you were having fun,

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:49.120
and it made us want to dance, too.

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:50.280
In that case, Sensei...

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:51.990
<b>Club Application</b>

00:21:52.300 --> 00:21:57.000
Hatoya... that wasn't literal. 
I don't want to join the association.

00:21:57.340 --> 00:21:59.660
It wasn't literal...

00:21:59.660 --> 00:22:02.890
Hatoya, stay. Stay!

00:23:38.600 --> 00:23:41.530
Next time: "The One on Top 
Is Scared of Heights!"
